   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to allowing\nmunicipalities to establish an adjustment percentage to be applied to the\nexemption percentage schedule for certain exemptions based upon permanent\npartial disabilities",
    "basePrintNo": "S8088",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8088-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §459-c, RPT L (as proposed in S.2574 & A.7164)",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8088\n\nSPONSOR: GOUNARDES\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to allowing muni-\ncipalities to establish an adjustment percentage to be applied to the\nexemption percentage schedule for certain exemptions based upon perma-\nnent partial disabilities\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of Chapter\n757 of the laws of 2023 that permits orders from the Workers' Compen-\nsation Board as proof of disability for the Disabled Homeowners'\nExemption (DHE).\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 makes technical and conforming changes to Section 459-c of the\nReal Property Tax Law.\n\nSection 2 provides for the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation provides for negotiated changes to the underlying\nlegislation to address technical concerns.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to Chapter 757 of the Laws of 2023. S.2574\npassed the Senate in March 2023 and A.7164 passed the Assembly in June\n2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNo Fiscal Impact.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2023 amending the real property tax law relating\nto tax exemptions for persons with disabilities, as proposed in legisla-\ntive bills numbers S. 2574 and A. 7164, takes effect.\n",
